course: dictionary
lesson: 13934
title: Lengthening: getting longer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lengthening means making something longer, or becoming longer. It comes from the word lengthen. «The days are lengthening as spring comes.» Each day has a little more light, so the days are getting longer.
explain: Lengthening can work as a verb, a noun, or an adjective. «The tailor is lengthening Sam's trousers.» is a verb: the tailor is making them longer. «The lengthening of the shadows told us it was evening.» is a noun: the process of getting longer. «The lengthening shadows crept across the grass.» is an adjective: shadows that are getting longer.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Ask: is something getting longer here? If so, lengthening fits. In «The shadows are lengthening at sunset», you can say «The shadows are getting longer at sunset» and it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Lengthening means making something longer, or becoming longer.
fact: «Lengthening» is the -ing form of the verb «lengthen».
fact: «Lengthening» can also be a noun, as in «the lengthening of the days».
fact: In spring, the days are lengthening, so the evenings get lighter for longer.
fact: In maths, lengthening one side of a shape changes its area.
exercise: «The tailor is lengthening the trousers for Sam.» What is the tailor doing to the trousers? | Washing them | Painting them | Making them shorter | *Making them longer
exercise: «In spring, the lengthening days bring warm sunshine.» What is lengthening here? | The sunshine is fading | *The days are getting longer | The sun is getting smaller | The days are getting colder
exercise: «At sunset the shadows were ___ across the field.» Which word fits the gap? | sleeping | *lengthening | cooking | shrinking
test: In maths, lengthening one side of a rectangle changes its area. What does lengthening mean? | Making a side shorter | Cutting off a corner | Painting a side | *Making a side longer
test: «Look at the lengthening shadows. It must be getting late.» What do the lengthening shadows show? | Shadows are turning black | *Shadows are getting longer | Shadows are getting shorter | Shadows have disappeared
exam: Which sentence uses lengthening as a noun? | *«The lengthening of the days is a sign of spring.» | «He was lengthening his stride.» | «The lengthening shadows are long.» | «She is lengthening the rope.»
